# Generate documentation images -- now scripts/doc_shots.py

# The doc screenshots are taken headlessly:
#
#   uv run python scripts/doc_shots.py            # all of them
#   uv run python scripts/doc_shots.py doc_08     # just the ones matching
#
# This script used to take them, and that is why ten of the images went
# unchanged from 2026-04-03 to 2026-10-28 while the toolbar's "?" button
# became "Help": running it needed a person to start termapy, connect to
# the demo device and type /run doc_screenshots, so nobody did.
#
# scripts/doc_shots.py boots the real app with app.run_test(), so the
# shots are one command and reproducible, and tests/test_doc_shots.py
# reddens when a committed image shows a toolbar the app no longer
# builds (registry doc-shots-current).  It also reaches three frames
# this script could not: while a script runs, the script-progress bar
# owns the toolbar, so the idle toolbar and the capture overlay never
# showed here.
#
# Still taken by hand, and listed in that script's MANUAL table: the
# command palette, both editors and the / popup.  The two pickers are
# scripts/doc_dialog_shots.py.  Quick Setup is a manual Ctrl+S.

/print Doc screenshots are now: uv run python scripts/doc_shots.py
